<p>Hmm. I like the premise but I feel like the logs are mostly repeating the same idea of regret over and over again without really expounding on it in a meaningful way. The first test log was interesting but the interviews only restated information already present in the description and the last notes felt flat. I think cutting everything after the testing log and expanding on those interactions would be much more enjoyable. I think there’s a lot more room in that space than we see here.</p>
<p>I also fixed a few formatting errors. Overall it’s a downvote from me right now but there’s potential here.</p>
<p>Oh also the redaction in the containment procedures spoils what are otherwise well thought-out and original procedures.</p>

